        {
          "url": "https://revvamplification.com/products/g2",
          "host": "revvamplification.com",
          "title": "REVV - G2 Anniversary Edition &ndash; Revv Amplification",
          "h1": "G2 Anniversary Edition",
          "description": "The Revv G2 was developed alongside Nashville&#39;s premier session guitarists to quickly achieve a wide variety of touch-sensitive edge-of-breakup amp; transparent crunch tones that satisfy the needs of the most demanding players. This brand-new V2 circuit revision carefully tweaked the bloom, sustain, amp; sag of notes for a true classic character across all gain ranges, amp; is available in a sleek Limited Edition enclosure amp; colorway.",
          "snippet": "REVV - G2 Anniversary Edition - Revv Amplification",
          "bodyExcerpt": "REVV - G2 Anniversary Edition &ndash; Revv Amplification Home About Gear Amplifiers Guitar Pedals Cabinets Custom Shop Artists Support Manuals Software Product Registration Dealers Find a Dealer Near You Become A Dealer Merch Clothing Accessories Demo/B-Stocks Contact Log in Search Instagram Menu Search Cart Home About Gear Amplifiers Guitar Pedals Cabinets Custom Shop Artists Support Manuals Software Product Registration Dealers Find a Dealer Near You Become A Dealer Merch Clothing Accessories Demo/B-Stocks Contact Log in Cart ( 0 ) Search Sale Off G2 Anniversary Edition ${{amount}} \" data-oldcurrency=\"USD\"> $229.00 $229.00 Save -2289900% The Revv G2 was developed alongside Nashville's premier session guitarists to quickly achieve a wide variety of touch-sensitive edge-of-breakup & transparent crunch tones that satisfy the needs of the most demanding players. This brand-new V2 circuit revision carefully tweaked the bloom, sustain, & sag of notes for a true classic character across all gain ranges. Quantity Add To Cart INFo & SPECS The Revv G2 was developed alongside Nashville's premier session guitarists to achieve a wide variety of touch-sensitive edge-of-breakup & transparent crunch tones that satisfy the needs of the most demanding players. This brand-new V2 circuit revision carefully tweaked the bloom, sustain, & sag of notes for a true classic character across all gain ranges. Features • Organic 'amp-in-a-box' pedal based on the G120 - Green channel • Tube-like crunch tones with great dynamics & clarity • 3 Position Drive switch for different voicing and gain saturation • Sounds great in front of an amp, or in the FX Loop as a pre-amp • Top-mounted jacks for convenience & saving space on your board • Built to tour ready quality standards • Custom Black enclosure w/anniversary graphics, and Green knobs • 1 in every 10 Pedals wins a prize! A t-shirt, a pedal, or an amp. Tech Specs Pedal: Analog/Digital: EQ: Inputs: Outputs: Power: Height: Width: Depth: Weight: Warranty: Overdrive Analog - True Bypass 3-band EQ 1 x 1/4\" 1 x 1/4\" 9V DC power, 14mA 1.25\" 2.75\" 4.7\" 0.8 lbs. 2 Year limited with registration RELATED ITEMS Sale Off Tilt Boost ${{amount}} \" data-oldcurrency=\"USD\"> $169.00 $169.00 Add To Cart David P. Top quality! AKIYOSHI N. Good! Colin B. Great pedal, real nice. Bob M. I'm a big fan of the G3 and G4 but had found myself leaning towards cleaner, edge-of-crunch sounds recently. The G2 Anniversary Edition might be the best &quot;amp in a box&quot; pedal I've ever owned. It has a really open, clear tone which, while sounding great on its own, stacks incredibly well with pedals earlier in the signal chain. I tend to set it to break up with digging in hard and use my guitars' volume knobs to clean up. If I need more dirt I'll hit it with an OD fuzz. Manages to make an old Peavey Bandit sound like a nice valve combo and makes night practice more fun using headphones and IRs. Pierre G. I use this pedal all the time since I got it. I also combine it with my G3 Anniversary. Great variety of sound coming from this pedal. Of all the pedals I have, they are the pedals I enjoy most. Dmytro P. Amazing pedals. All of them G2, G3, G4. These pedals form sound completely like a reap amplifier. You just need to add Cabinet simulator and some reverb if you want. Also they take TS 808 like a real tube amp. Jeremy R. Love it!! Kevin W. I love the sound of the pedal. I did gat a second one through a music store that had a great deal on them. Strangel, the two pedals sound different with the same settings... one has more headroom before it breaks up, while the other has a better bass response... (I like the bass response in my pedals...). I would give the pedal a 5 if not for the slight hiss with the signal compared to the V1 G2. It's more like a 4.8 out of 5. Stay In Touch Want to know about new discounts & gear? Sign up for our zero-spam mailing list! Email Subscribe Menu Return Policy Privacy Policy Warranty Registration Term & Condi",
