          "snippet": "Fuzzface Variants | Fuzz | Angel Face | Skreddy Pedals",
          "bodyExcerpt": "Fuzzface Variants | Fuzz | Angel Face | Skreddy Pedals (function(w,d,s,l,i){w[l]=w[l]||[];w[l].push({'gtm.start': new Date().getTime(),event:'gtm.js'});var f=d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0], j=d.createElement(s),dl=l!='dataLayer'?'&l='+l:'';j.async=true;j.src= 'https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtm.js?id='+i+dl;f.parentNode.insertBefore(j,f); })(window,document,'script','dataLayer','AW-972332178'); / / Account \"> Cart Skreddy Pedals Home Effect Types Boost Overdrive Fuzz Delay Modulation Octave Utilities all Manufacturers \"> News Artists Dealers About Skreddy Pedals Animals Pedal Tee Shirt Information Terms and Conditions Cookie Policy Privacy Policy \"> Sign In Remember Me Sign In New customers click here Lost your password? Home Effect Types Fuzz Fuzzface Variants Angel Face Angel Face Classic Fuzz Face, best for humbuckers Aimed at that elusive first-generation fuzz tone made most famous by Hendrix This can be a smooth saturated fuzz or an articulate fuzz, depending on how you set it up. The bias control will give you just the right classic response at noon, and you can play with it to go harder or softer. read more reviews clips SKU: AngelFace-deposit MPN: SKR-ANGF Stock Status: Preorder Delivery Status: Lead time of about 2 weeks We build everything to order. Our current wait time is approximately 2 weeks to 1 month. I will confirm your order shortly, and I will send you a PayPal invoice for the total amount due including shipping when your order is ready. --Marc Price: $259 + shipping $259 $233.10 (10% off) 50% deposit $116.55 Quantity qty Add To Cart Classic Oldschool Fuzz Reviews • Clips • Manual The Skreddy Pedals™ Angel Face is made from silicon transistors for stability, but it uses low gain units that can render germanium type fuzz tones. The extra controls let you emulate different classic fuzz tones from the 60's and early 70's along with improvements for some of the issues those early fuzzes had (noise reduction, adjustable tone, and adjustable input resistance). No special power requirements, just regular negative ground 9v. Classic Fuzz Tones Responsive and raw just like the earliest units Adjustible input resistance lets it work great with humbuckers and get along with other effects too Stable at all temperatures but very sensitive to guitar volume knob changes Just leave the fuzz knob cranked or backed down a touch True bypass, LED, standard 9v power jack Controls: VOLUME Gives you more output volume than most classic fuzzes, with unity gain around noon and plenty of boost beyond that. BIAS Lets you go from buzzy and low-fi to clear, louder, and more present. Sometimes referred to as a \"MIDS\" control since it does give you more (or less) of those too. Noon is the classic setting. VOICE Lets you go from bright and articulate to smooth and syrupy with that lovely upper-harmonic emphasis you hear in classic fuzz recordings. It's really nothing more than an extra guitar tone control. This fuzz sounds so sweet with the tone rolled down that you will love having this dedicated control right where it's at, freeing up the guitar knobs for all your other applications. FUZZ Sets the gain for this whole thing. Most fuzzes of this type sound best with the fuzz turned either all the way up or dialed back just a touch from max (in my opinion). Gets milder and darker as you turn down. HOT Adds a little or a lot of resistance to the input in order to keep a humbucker pickup from swamping the circuit and causing it to have a gated attack. But it's also useful for helping this fuzz work together with other effects (like to keep a wah pedal from making that siren sound you get from driving it into a vintage-style fuzz, or that extreme, trebly fuzz you get if you use a buffered pedal in front, for example). Sound Clips Quick clip I recorded Using a Strat: bypassed first, then Angel Face, then adding Echo, then adding Little Miss Sunshine out front to show how it gets along great with the phaser in front (video) Skreddy Angel Face wi",
