          "snippet": "Skreddy Pedals Juicy Pig Fuzz | Fuzz - durableguitars.com",
          "bodyExcerpt": "Skreddy Pedals Juicy Pig Fuzz | Fuzz Acoustic guitars Bass guitars Electric guitars Classical guitars New Arrivals Checkout Cart(0) Home &#47; Fuzz &#47; Skreddy Pedals Juicy Pig Fuzz Skreddy Pedals Juicy Pig Fuzz SKU: X345904281 Category: Fuzz &#36; 214.00 Original price was: &#036;214.00. &#36; 107.00 Current price is: &#036;107.00. Skreddy Pedals Juicy Pig Fuzz quantity Add to cart Description Maker: Skreddy Pedals Model: Juicy Pig Condition: New Description: Transparent, powerful, dynamic fuzz that sustains the note and maintains clarity The Skreddy Pedals Juicy Pig is another modification of the circa 1976 &#8220;rams head&#8221; Big Muff Pi*. It is designed to enhance the clarity of the signal to provide all the gain and sustain of the original but with less buzz-saw grind and more amp-like transparency. Works even better with humbucker-equipped guitars; features a less-tightened low end, more natural frequency response, and more of a liquid sustain that grabs the guitar&#8217;s frequency characteristic instead of adding its own * The term &#8220;Big Muff Pi&#8221; is only being used for comparison and is owned by our lovely friends at Electro-Harmonix who invented the circuit and built its worthy reputation Sustain and power with better transparency and less buzz-saw grind than a typical muff design This pig will propel your playing and sounds more like an amp on the edge of meltdown than a fuzz pedal. Near-endless sustain coupled with detailed string articulation and low-end transparency, melds with and bonds with your essential guitar tone, sustains and compresses yet sounds dynamic too. Power Regular 9v negative ground, no special power requirements. 9v battery is not included. If you use a battery, then remember to un-plug the input cable from the pedals input jack when not in use to prevent draining (or you can also just plug in a power-supply, which disconnects the battery). You may supply external power through an AC adapter. 