          "bodyExcerpt": "Skreddy Pedals P19 | Effects Database Skip to navigation Brands &#9660; 0-9... a... b... c... d... e... f... g... h... i... j... k... l... m... n... o... p... q... r... s... t... u... v... w... x... y... z... Effect types &#9660; boost distortion fuzz overdrive acoustic simulation amp simulation speaker/cabinet simulation chorus flanger phaser tremolo vibe vibrato other modulation pitch shifter octaver delay reverb looper/sampler hold/freeze eq filter wah fuzz-wah bitcrusher ring modulator samplerate reducer wavefolder synth effect granular effect multi effect vocal effect talkbox vocoder buffer compressor other... Countries &#9660; (country unknown) Argentina Australia Austria Belarus Belgium Brazil Bulgaria Canada Chile China Colombia Costa Rica Croatia Czech Republic Czechoslovakia DDR Denmark Dominican Republic Ecuador Egypt Estonia Finland France Germany Greece Hungary India Indonesia Iran Ireland Israel Italy Japan Latvia Lithuania Luxembourg Macedonia Malaysia Malta Mexico Moldova Monaco Morocco Netherlands New-Zealand Norway Panama Peru Philippines Poland Portugal Romania Russia Serbia Singapore Slovakia Slovenia South-Africa South-Korea Spain Sweden Switzerland Taiwan Thailand Turkey U.K. U.S.A. U.S.S.R. Ukraine Uruguay Venezuela Browse by &#9660; Enclosure type Modulation type Special &#9658; Classics Eye candy Funny Vaporware Weird Random brand Random effect Events &#9658; NAMM Musikmesse Music China Guitar Summit More... &#9660; Forum (opens in new tab) myFXDB (opens in new tab) Newsletter About How to get listed? Interviews Reviews Effects explained Books D.I.Y. Schematics Links Contact Install Effects Database App Search the database browse by brand S... Skreddy Pedals browse by type distortion/fuzz/overdrive fuzz browse by enclosure pedal Skreddy Pedals P19 Published on January 27, 2012 Skreddy Pedals fuzz pedal Information The Skreddy Pedals P19 is a fuzz pedal inspired by the iconic guitar tones of Pink Floyd's 1979 album The Wall . Based on a modified Big Muff circuit, it was designed to deliver smooth, soaring sustain with exceptional clarity and articulation, avoiding the muddiness and excessive fizz often associated with high-gain fuzz designs. The P19 balances its EQ response by slightly scooping the mids to prevent congestion, rolling off low frequencies to reduce boominess, and shaping the highs to remain present without harshness. This tuning makes it particularly well-suited for sustaining lead tones that cut through a mix while retaining a creamy, musical quality. A key feature of the pedal is its mid-voicing switch, which provides two tonal options: a flat setting with a subtle scoop for clarity, or a hump setting that boosts midrange frequencies for added thickness, juiciness, and presence. This versatility allows the P19 to shift between articulate solo tones and fuller, more saturated sounds. Designed as a high-gain but low-noise fuzz, the P19 excels at sustaining, biting, legato lead work while still offering enough dynamic response to remain expressive. Controls Volume : Adjusts the overall output level Sustain : Controls the amount of fuzz and sustain Tone : Shapes the EQ balance between bass and treble Flat/Hump Switch : Selects between a subtle mid scoop (flat) and a boosted midrange (hump) Technical Specifications Circuit: Big Muff-style fuzz with modified EQ Power: Standard 9V DC power supply; confirmed to operate up to 18V for increased headroom Construction: Aluminum enclosure Dimensions: approx. 3\" wide x 5\" deep x 1\" tall Highlights Designed to capture the sustaining lead tones of Pink Floyd's The Wall Big Muff-based fuzz tuned for clarity and articulation Balanced EQ with controlled lows, scooped mids, and smooth highs Mid-voicing switch for flat or boosted midrange response High gain, low noise design optimized for expressive lead work Video Date &#x25BC;&#x25B2; Maker &#x25BC;&#x25B2; Video &#x25BC;&#x25B2; Time &#x25BC;&#x25B2; 2013-12-17 BjornRiis Skreddy Pedals P19 review 4:00 20",
