e among Big Muff afficionados. The Skreddy Pedals™ Perestroika hearkens to the early 1990's Russian tank version fuzz which had a gritty bite to the top end, a smooth, gently scooped midrange, and a warm, but not boomy low end. Okay, it can get boomy. Depending on where you set the tone control. Has just enough gain to propel your solos and never mushy on chords. We're adding our customary midrange boost mini toggle, too, for flat mids, no scoop! There are a limited number of transistors we can make them with, but we don't foresee running out any time soon. I just couldn't handle the lack of sustain in the stock version. I had to add just a TINY bit more \"zing\" and creamy sustain so it would be useful for soloing. But I did not get rid of the characteristic bass clean blend that is a hallmark of the green/civil war Russians. Video Date &#x25BC;&#x25B2; Maker &#x25BC;&#x25B2; Video &#x25BC;&#x25B2; Time &#x25BC;&#x25B2; 2017-07-21 drowninginguitars Skreddy Perestroika Fuzz Demo 2:17 2015-08-03 9520575 Skreddy Perestroika 3:25 Reviews myFXDB user reviews No reviews yet + Add your review Links Skreddy Pedals Skreddy Pedals Perestroika Related Electro-Harmonix Axis Manlay Sound XS Fuzz Electro-Harmonix Big Muff Pi Lyle L600 Distortion Sustainer (made by EH) Marveltone Distortion Sustainer (made by EH) Wabash Distortion Sustainer (made by EH) (unknown, Japan) Big Mag Sustainar (vintage Japanese copy) Electro Sound Co. Big Muff Sustainar (vintage Japanese copy) Elk Big Muff Sustainar (vintage Japanese copy) EarthQuaker Devices Hizumitas - Fuzz Sustainar (copy of Elk BM Sustainar) Elk ES-960 Super Fuzz Sustainar (vintage Japanese copy) Elk SFS-1 Super Fuzz Sustainar (reissue) Wren and Cuff The White Elk - Super Fuzz Sustainer (copy of the Elk Super Fuzz Sustainar) Hohner MF-50 Tri Dirty Booster (vintage US copy) Maccanbell Big Muff Sustainar (vintage Japanese copy) Pro/Watt Reventador (vintage Argentinian copy) Sekova SE-2015 Big Muff (vintage Japanese copy) Mike Matthew