        {
          "url": "https://guitar.com/news/gear-news/skreddy-pedals-rubber-soul-is-a-fab-four-inspired-preamp-stompbox/",
          "host": "guitar.com",
          "title": "Skreddy Pedals’ Rubber Soul is a Fab Four-inspired preamp stompbox | Guitar.com",
          "h1": "Skreddy Pedals’ Rubber Soul is a Fab Four-inspired preamp stompbox",
          "description": "Get close to the sound and feel of a small British tube combo.",
          "snippet": "Skreddy Pedals&#x27; Rubber Soul is a fab four-inspired preamp stompbox",
          "bodyExcerpt": "Skreddy Pedals’ Rubber Soul is a Fab Four-inspired preamp stompbox | Guitar.com News Reviews Guides Features Magazine Tuner Deals Related Brands Skreddy Pedals Related Tags # Distortion # Effects When you purchase through affiliate links on Guitar.com, you may contribute to our site through commissions. Learn more Featured Deal Fender American Professional II Telecaster – save $200! Claim News Skreddy Pedals’ Rubber Soul is a Fab Four-inspired preamp stompbox Get close to the sound and feel of a small British tube combo. by Daniel Ong April 24, 2019 by Daniel Ong April 24, 2019 When you purchase through affiliate links on Guitar.com, you may contribute to our site through commissions. Learn more Get Guitar.com breaking news as it happens by following us on Telegram: https://t.me/guitardotcom Skreddy Pedals’ has unveiled Rubber Soul, a guitar preamp pedal modelled after a small British tube combo. It was designed to deliver a sound reminiscent of rock’s golden years, channelling The Beatles, Rory Gallagher, Queen and more. According to the brand, the pedal can take your tone from “clean to hot and jangly to smoky, slightly ragged overdrive”. It also has a two-band EQ that can be tweaked to achieve mid scoop, mid hump, bright, dark, thin and fat tones. This is bolstered by an optical compressor circuit designed to emulate a sagging GZ34 tube rectifier, a saturated output transformer, overloaded voice coils and speaker cones. All of these elements aim to provide the complete small combo experience. Available at $239. More info at skreddypedals.com . Related Brands Skreddy Pedals Related Tags # Distortion # Effects Trending Now 1 What is a PLEK machine anyway? And can it really make your guitar play and feel better? 2 “It was just so difficult and insane” Joe Satriani tells the story of his favourite guitar solo 3 Why Martin’s 16 Series is its most interesting new range in years 4 Fender Telecaster: 75 Years Of History Join Our Mailing List Get Exclusive Deals Sign Up Now The destination for all things guitar Privacy Policy Cookie Notice Terms of use Advertise Contact © 2026 Guitar.com is part of NME Networks .",
